title: lirael_17th_hour
tags: character:Lirael moon:1 beat:climax
---
<<tag character:Lirael>>
Lirael: You came. I knew it would be you — I heard the song change at the seventeenth bell.
Lirael: Most people only feel the hum. You... you tuned it. You made the stones remember their own voice.
Lirael: That makes you the one mother said would come. The one who could wake the song without breaking it.
Lirael: Three buildings. Three notes. Telluric for the ground, Harmonic for the heart, Celestial for the sky.
Lirael: That wasn't a puzzle. That was a key. The first key of twelve, and every one is buried under a different moon.
Lirael: When the cathedral light went up, somewhere far away another sleeper rolled over in her dream.
Lirael: The prophecy isn't a story written down. It's a chord. You just played its opening.
Lirael: My mother is Anastasia. She's the one who taught me to listen for the bells underneath the bells.
Lirael: She's been sleeping a long time. Not the kind of sleeping you wake from by shaking — the kind the moons themselves have to agree to end.
Lirael: There are others like her. Twelve, scattered across the moons that still turn above us.
Lirael: Some of them are waiting. Some of them are dreaming things they don't want to leave. Some of them might fight you for waking them at all.
Lirael: I can't stay. The light up there — it's already pulling me to where I'm supposed to be next.
Lirael: But listen. Twelve more wait. Some won't want to wake. Find me again under the next moon.
Lirael: I'll leave a song behind so you know which way to walk. You'll hear it when the wind changes.
Lirael: Goodbye, tuner. Don't be afraid of what you started here tonight.
===
